note bay 5 review of b203fc8c (same class as x-sleepneg): symlnk on a packet with one record (two are required) traps 3 before
note any kernel call (OMEGESE s10); ngrun refuses symlnk (121) only after that check.
fn main to int
a = new uchar 5 0
put a 0 1
put a 2 1
put a 4 97
k = symlnk a 0 5
ret int and k 255
end
